      "message": "Review agent shows:\n\n```\nThe condition `++resolved_count_ \u003d\u003d defined_count_` can be true multiple times during a single GN run. Every time a set of targets is resolved and the loader is momentarily caught up, this will fire. \n\nAs a result, the callback in `command_gen.cc` will be called multiple times, each time scheduling work for the *entire* list of targets collected so far. This leads to redundant metadata walks and file writing tasks.\n\nA better approach would be to remove these counters and the callback from `Builder`, and instead have `command_gen.cc` call a \"write generated files\" function exactly once after `setup-\u003eRun()` has finished successfully. The `Builder` can still maintain the `generated_file_targets_` list and provide a getter for it.\n```\n\nI think this is true, I need to find a better condition. The current implementation is correct but does too much work.",
